-- title:
--   Integrality of q-expansions of global 1-forms on a ℤ₍ₚ₎-model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$, a prime $p$ with $p\nmid N$, and a ring embedding $\iota_0$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ into $\mathbf C$, and write $R$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbf Q$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ with $X$ integral, and let $\mathcal V$ consist of two affine opens $U_0, U_1$ covering $X$ with affine intersection. The data are: a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbf Q$ of the field $F_N \subset \mathbf Q((q))$ generated by the expansions $q\mapsto j(q^d)$, $d\mid N$, together with an isomorphism $e_0$ of $M_0.C$ with the base change of $c$ along $R\to\mathbf Q$ compatible with the structure morphisms, whose generic point lies over $U_0$; a ring homomorphism $\iota : \Gamma(X,U_0)\to \bar F_N$ (the subfield of $\overline{\mathbf Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of $F_N$) given on sections by transporting the germ at the generic point through $M_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ and the coefficient embedding, and restricting on $R$ to $R\to\overline{\mathbf Q}\to\bar F_N$; an additive map $\mathrm{res}$ from $H^0$ of the Kähler sections of the cover (pairs of relative differentials on $\Gamma(X,U_0)$, $\Gamma(X,U_1)$ agreeing on the overlap) to $\Omega[\bar F_N/\overline{\mathbf Q}]$, equal on each element to the image of its first component under the semilinear map induced by $(R\to\overline{\mathbf Q}, \iota)$; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$ and a $\mathbf Q$-point $y$ of the base change lying over $\varepsilon_\infty$, carried by $e_0^{-1}$ to a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose place is the cusp $\infty$ of $F_N$; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ of $\bar F_N$ isomorphic, compatibly, to the base change of $c$ along $R\to\overline{\mathbf Q}$, subject to equivariance of its point–place bijection for the arithmetic Galois action (hypothesis `hgal`) and to the condition that the place of a $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-point of $M_\eta$, restricted along $F_N\to\overline{\mathbf Q}\otimes_{\mathbf Q} F_N \cong \bar F_N$, is the place of the closed point of $M_0$ below it (hypothesis `hcompat`); and, for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, a lift $\rho$ of $R\to\overline{\mathbf Q}$ to $A$, a curve model $M_A$ over the residue field of $A$ of the corresponding modular function field, isomorphic compatibly to the base change of $c$ along $R\to A\to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and (for algebraically closed residue field) a degree-preserving reduction map $r$ of places mod the maximal ideal of $A$ compatible with specialisation of points of $M_\eta$ to points of $M_A$. Then for every $\omega \in H^0$ of the Kähler sections there is a power series $P$ with coefficients in $R$ such that the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{diffQExpBar}_N(\mathrm{res}\,\omega)$ is the Laurent series attached to the image of $P$ under $R\to\overline{\mathbf Q}$.
--
--   This is the integrality of $q$-expansions of global relative $1$-forms on a smooth proper model of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$: such a form has $q$-expansion at the rational cusp $\infty$ lying in $\mathbf Z_{(p)}[[q]]$, in particular of non-negative order. It is used in the identification of $H^0(X,\Omega^1_{X/R})$ with the integral lattice of cusp forms of level $N$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_powerSeries_diffQExpBar_eq_ofPowerSeries_map_of_kaehlerH0_of_ratCurveModel_of_cuspSection_compat_of_neZero.lean

